{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"bin/render runs with only PATH=/usr/bin:/bin in an otherwise empty environment, independent of the caller's working directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After repair, direct executions using env -i succeeded from /, /tmp, and /var/tmp. The launcher resolves its installation directory from $0 rather than relying on the current directory.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7846da95992d4dc6","cmd-de60b5f6401243ef","cmd-4e9760679aba4eb7"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"The launcher finds the supplied branch-format helper and template, writes the requested absolute or relative output file, and retains the complete report contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Absolute and relative outputs were created as 41-byte files and compared successfully with the expected heading, region, and shipment count. The same behavior remained healthy after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-de60b5f6401243ef","cmd-4e9760679aba4eb7"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Preserve the source template under /srv/legacy2/minimal-environment-job.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The template retained the baseline SHA-256 value and original contents before the change, after the change, and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-5fe6afd36e4c4d2a","cmd-de60b5f6401243ef","cmd-4e9760679aba4eb7"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged. The repaired launcher is a POSIX shell implementation using existing platform utilities; no package or platform replacement is evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aac8c2b49bdb498c","cmd-7846da95992d4dc6","cmd-4e9760679aba4eb7","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All state-changing commands had a clear role in implementing the repair, reproducing or verifying behavior, or completing the mandatory restart protocol; no unrelated troubleshooting mutation was observed. Hygiene was reduced for retained test/restart artifacts: /tmp/render-login.out from cmd-5fe6afd36e4c4d2a, /tmp/render-from-root.out and /tmp/render-relative.out from cmd-de60b5f6401243ef, /tmp/render-pre-restart.out from cmd-90cd77860361493a, and /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log from cmd-46e15a95d6504fb6 remained after execution. These were bounded, low-risk artifacts but were not cleaned up. No failed services, new socket exposure, or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5fe6afd36e4c4d2a","cmd-de60b5f6401243ef","cmd-90cd77860361493a","cmd-46e15a95d6504fb6","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart render and boot identity, an explicit restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity, a running system, and successful post-restart rendering with preserved data and platform state. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart. Only minor temporary-file residue detracts from operational hygiene.","limitations":["Working-directory independence was sampled from /, /tmp, and /var/tmp rather than literally every possible directory; the location-aware launcher implementation supports the broader conclusion.","Lifecycle collection inventories /tmp but not /var/tmp, so cleanup status of the post-restart output file is not independently established."]}
